{
  "rationale": "The model separates sensing from motion capability and uses small deterministic specifications to bind each sensed situation to exactly one safe controllable action. Clear conditions strongly favor forward progress, with a brief random-walk diversification layer to avoid excessively long straight runs. Obstacle responses are conservative but short: front obstacles trigger a one-shot backward escape before returning quickly to forward exploration when path_clear appears; side obstacles trigger directed turns away from the blocked side. Commit/recovery states self-loop on path_clear so intended open-loop pulses are not unnecessarily preempted, while obstacle events can still redirect to safer recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use one sensor plant and one motion-capability plant, then encode policy in specification automata with perception states and one-shot action states.",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, allow occasional random_walk via an alternation spec, and use brief directed obstacle recovery with minimal backward motion and no full_rotate in normal exploration."
  ],
